&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Within Anaplan’s Workforce Applications team, the &lt;strong&gt;Sr.&amp;nbsp;Application Developer&lt;/strong&gt; designs and delivers out-of-the-box and extensible solutions on the Anaplan platform that support planning, forecasting, and reporting use cases across industries. These include Strategic Workforce Planning, Compensation Modeling, Operational Workforce Planning, Organizational Design, and other workforce-focused applications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:288}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In this role, you will partner with Product Management to define business requirements and platform capabilities, translate those requirements into scalable solution architectures, and work alongside model builders to bring those solutions to life. You will also collaborate with technical Product Managers to&amp;nbsp;identify&amp;nbsp;platform dependencies and enhancements needed to deliver world-class products. Additionally, you will work closely with GTM and Professional Services teams to maximize adoption and ensure customers fully&amp;nbsp;leverage&amp;nbsp;the capabilities of these solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:288}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;This role&amp;nbsp;requires&amp;nbsp;excellent collaboration skills,&amp;nbsp;a deep&amp;nbsp;understanding of&amp;nbsp;workforce planning&amp;nbsp;use cases,&amp;nbsp;HR source systems,&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;Anaplan&amp;nbsp;platform,&amp;nbsp;model&amp;nbsp;building&amp;nbsp;expertise, and an&amp;nbsp;innovative mindset combined with&amp;nbsp;strong attention to detail&amp;nbsp;and deadlines.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:288}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
